# Solution to PUZZLE 5. The 3rd harmonic gets volume 1 and the
# rest keep a quieter saw-like 0.3/n, so the fundamental is
# still there. A formant bump works too:
#   def my_shape(n, pf): (1 / n) * (1 + exp(-pow((pf - 600) / 80, 2)) * 8)
#
#@ top 600 5 -- the 3rd harmonic (600 Hz) is the loudest
#@ peak 200 4 -30 -- the 200 Hz fundamental is still there

def my_shape(n, pf): if n == 3 then 1.0 else 0.3 / n

play singer:
  additive(200, my_shape, 8) * 0.2

singer
